  <dialog id="controls-dialog" class="wide-dialog"><div class="dialog-top"><span class="eyebrow">FIELD MANUAL</span><button class="close-dialog icon-button" aria-label="Close controls">×</button></div><h2>Know your tools.</h2><div class="controls-grid"><section><h3>Movement</h3><dl><dt>W A S D</dt><dd>Move</dd><dt>MOUSE / ARROWS</dt><dd>Look around</dd><dt>SPACE</dt><dd>Jump. Press again in the air to leap.</dd><dt>SHIFT</dt><dd>Surge in your move direction</dd><dt>E</dt><dd>Use the nearest device</dd><dt>M / TAB</dt><dd>Open mission map</dd><dt>ESC / P</dt><dd>Pause</dd></dl></section><section><h3>Combat</h3><dl><dt>LEFT MOUSE</dt><dd>Fire carbine or strike with blade</dd><dt>RIGHT MOUSE</dt><dd>Guard with blade. Time it to return a bolt.</dd><dt>Q</dt><dd>Pulse. Push enemies, return bolts, and charge coils.</dd><dt>1 / 2 / WHEEL</dt><dd>Select carbine or blade</dd><dt>R</dt><dd>Reload carbine</dd><dt>F</dt><dd>Enter or leave full screen</dd></dl></section></div><div class="manual-note"><strong>Watch the light.</strong><p>Cyan marks your route and working devices. Red marks an attack. Amber marks an archive or supply cache.</p><p>A blade strike opens damaged grilles. An air leap reaches high ledges. Resonance recovers after use.</p></div><div class="dialog-bottom"><span class="field-help">If mouse capture is unavailable, drag to look or use the arrow keys.</span><button class="close-dialog primary small">Ready</button></div></dialog>
